From b9546117c169ca30d999647190ad0f5da143525d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 02:49:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] krans: signed previous-byte contexts, run-coded context
 map, 16-bit word contexts; SPEC text for codec 33

Measured on the residual leaves of astronaut.ppm / coffee.ppm (rc3 balanced leaf 431,788 / 451,631):
the previous channel's residual with its sign as context (bq 3, 11 bins) 368,874 -> 353,320 and
383,639 -> 362,896; a finer set of signed bins or a second previous channel moved the result by
under 1% and are not in the format. The context map is coded with a 'same table as the context
before' bit (unused contexts cost one bit; 600 bytes of text: 306 -> 217 bytes coded). Image
leaves use 2 MiB chunks (retina 1,005,562 -> 1,002,227, hubble 1,434,052 -> 1,430,702 against
1 MiB). mk 3: pairs of bytes as 16-bit zigzag words, the lag terms are half-octave classes of
the neighbouring words (for the 16-bit image claim; mr block 3: 253,790 against zstd's 288,977).
eq 3: 48 linear bins. One context buffer is shared by the trials (4 bytes of scratch per chunk
byte instead of 6).

