@@ -489,6 +491,35 @@ them; a zero literal, a run past `rl` or bytes left over in either stream is an
 **Plane-aligned Huffman and rANS chunks** (codecs 13 and 14 cut at plane boundaries, one-symbol rANS chunks) are
 ordinary codec 13/14 leaves and need no version; from rc3 the encoder tries them by default at `hc`.
 
+**Leaf codec 33: context rANS (version 11; written only with `KOLMO_NATIVE=rans`).** Kolmo's own static rANS coder
+with static contexts (`src/algo/krans.c`; the normative text is the header comment of `src/algo/krans.h`). A leaf is a
+run of independent chunks up to its raw length. Chunk: `kind` u8, raw length `m` uv (1 to 2^24), then for kind 0 the
+`m` bytes, for kind 1 one byte repeated `m` times, for kind 2:
+
+- `b0`: bits 0–2 log2 of the state count S (0–5), bits 3–5 the phase period P − 1 (P = 1–8), bits 6–7 the mantissa
+  bits of the tables (3, 4, 6 or 12); `b1`: bits 0–1 `eq`, bits 2–3 `bq`, bits 4–5 `mk`, bit 6 `pf`, bit 7 zero;
+  if `eq` ≠ 0 a lag count (1–4) and each lag uv (1 to 2^24); then T − 1 u8 (T tables, T ≤ N, T ≤ 1 + m / 16);
+- a bit stream (least significant bit first, zero-padded to a byte): the context map (when T > 1, per context one
+  bit: 1 = the table of the context before it, 0 = followed by the table index in ⌈log2 T⌉ bits), then T tables
+  (first and last present symbol, 8 bits each; per symbol between them a class, prefix-coded against the previous
+  class: `0` same, `10` −1, `110` +1, `1110` −2, `11110` +2, `11111` and 4 bits explicit; class 0 absent, class
+  e ≥ 1 a frequency in [2^(e−1), 2^e) followed by the min(e − 1, mantissa bits) bits below its top bit; explicit
+  class 14 marks the one symbol that takes what the others leave of 2^12);
+- coded length `z` uv, then S states (32 bits little-endian) and the 16-bit little-endian words.
+
+The chunk is cut into S contiguous segments of ⌊m / S⌋ bytes (the last also takes the remainder); state k decodes
+segment k, one byte of each segment in turn, then the remainder. A byte at position i of its segment and j of the
+chunk has context `(QE[e] · NB + QB[prev]) · P + (j mod P)`: `e` is the sum of the magnitudes of the bytes at
+i − lag (0 for lags before the segment start) binned by `eq` (0: no lags, one bin; 1: 17 bins, edges 1 2 4 6 8 11
+14 18 23 29 37 47 60 80 110 160; 2: 9 bins, edges 1 3 6 11 18 29 47 80); `prev` is the byte at i − 1 (0 at the
+segment start; not used in phase 0 when `pf` is set) binned by `bq` (0: none; 1: the byte itself, 256 bins; 2: its
+magnitude with edges 1 3 6 12 25, 6 bins; 3: the same with the sign, 11 bins); the magnitude of a byte b is by `mk`
+(b + 1) >> 1 with odd b negative (zigzag residuals), min(b, 256 − b) with b ≥ 128 negative, or b. N = NE · NB · P
+is at most 4096. Decoding a symbol with state x and the context's table: slot = x mod 2^12, the symbol whose range
+[c, c + f) holds the slot, x = f · ⌊x / 2^12⌋ + slot − c, and while x < 2^16 one word is appended below it. A chunk
+is valid only when every state ends at 2^16 and the words are used up exactly; reserved values, a table that leaves
+nothing for its class-14 symbol, non-zero padding and trailing bytes are refused.
+
